Q: Does my code look secure? And How do I prevent people from entering a page? A: <p>I would recommend hashing passwords instead of keeping them as plain text in the database. Storing passwords as plain text in the database is not good practice as if the database was compromised all the passwords are clearly readable. You could store the password as a hash using something like the following --&gt;</p>
<pre><code>$plainPassword = $_POST['pwd'] ?? '';
$hash = password_hash($plainPassword, PASSWORD_DEFAULT);
// store $hash in the pwd column
</code></pre>

Q: How to enable captions by default in Vimeo showcase embed A: <p>According to the Vimeo Support Team, this is impossible at the moment (April 2024):</p>
<blockquote>
<p>According to the development team, this is expected behavior, and that
showcases do not support the texttrack query param, just the
videos.</p>
<p>I will open a feedback request to our product team to
consider adding this behavior in the future if possible.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>One solution is to have an iframe showing the first video, with captions enabled by default, and move to the next video in the showcase with JavaScript. Here is the code for this case in HTML:</p>
<pre class="lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;iframe id=&quot;cumulative_looper_video&quot; src=&quot;https://player.vimeo.com/video/76979871?texttrack=fr&quot; width=&quot;640&quot; height=&quot;360&quot; frameborder=&quot;0&quot; allow=&quot;autoplay; fullscreen&quot; allowfullscreen&gt;&lt;/iframe&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>and in JavaScript:</p>
<pre><code>const looper_video_ids = [
  922184512,
  922182160,
  922182277,
  922182416,
  922182488,
  922182673,
  922182872,
  922183046,
  922183202,
  922183262,
  922183396,
  922183483,
  922183537,
  922183644,
  922183796,
  922183863,
  922183912,
  922184015,
  922184146,
  922184617,
  922184208,
];

var cumulative_looper_index = 0;

var cumulative_looper_iframe = document.querySelector(&quot;iframe#cumulative_looper_video&quot;);

var cumulative_looper_player = new Vimeo.Player(cumulative_looper_iframe);


var cumulative_looper_play = function() {
  cumulative_looper_player.play();
  if (vimeo_caption_language_container) {
    cumulative_looper_player.enableTextTrack(&quot;fr&quot;);
  }
}

var on_cumulative_looper_end = function(data) {

  cumulative_looper_index += 1;

  // For safety, make sure the song index goes back to zero.
  if (looper_video_ids.length &lt;= cumulative_looper_index) {
    cumulative_looper_index = 0;
  }
  let new_video_id = looper_video_ids[cumulative_looper_index];

  // Load new video.
  cumulative_looper_player.loadVideo(new_video_id).then(function() {
    cumulative_looper_play();
    setTimeout(cumulative_looper_play, 500);
  });
});

cumulative_looper_player.on(&quot;ended&quot;, on_cumulative_looper_end);
</code></pre>

Q: How to change a MySQL column name that has # (Hash) symbol A: <p>Use backticks:</p>
<pre><code>CREATE TABLE test (`Grade#Final#Exam` DOUBLE);

DESCRIBE test;

ALTER TABLE test CHANGE `Grade#Final#Exam` GradeFinalExam DOUBLE;

DESCRIBE test;
</code></pre>
